+# Size check (before Phase 1 questions)
+
+Run once per goal, before the Phase 1 MCQs, from the request and the files it names. Never block on it; when unsure, answer `no` and route `full`.
+
+## Rubric
+
+The route is `lite` only when all four hold:
+
+- (a) At most 3 files are expected to change.
+- (b) No new or changed shared interface: exported signature, schema, CLI flag, config key or file format consumed by other modules.
+- (c) No new dependency.
+- (d) No destructive, security or infrastructure surface.
+
+Log the four answers and the route in one line; the line is their only record:
+
+`_kit/log-spawn.sh note --goal [goal] --text "size-check: a=<yes|no> b=<yes|no> c=<yes|no> d=<yes|no> route=<lite|full>"`
+
+Run it once `_memory/work/goals/<goal>/` exists; until then keep the line and log it with the Phase 2 `note`s. `goal.md` records only the route, as a `route: full|lite` key in the `phases:` block.
+
+## Routes
+
+**full** — the phases as written in `SKILL.md`.
+
+**lite** — for a `route: lite` goal this file replaces the Phase 3 gate and the Phase 5 audit. Phase 1 confirmation is as in `SKILL.md`, then:
+
+- Phase 2 writes one task file with `## Acceptance Criteria` and no separate final test task.
+- Pre-flight (`reference/preflight.md`, including trace-lint) runs after Phase 2 and before Phase 4, as on the full route otherwise.
+- No Phase 3 goal evaluation.
+- Phase 4 runs one `implementer` and one `evaluator`. The task's Phase 4 PASS satisfies the iron rule that no phase advances without evaluator approval. Fix cycles, their cap and the continuation ladder apply as on the full route.
+- No separate Phase 5 audit. The task's Phase 4 PASS plus the Quality Checks (rung 3, via spawned `terminal`) is the goal's final approval: run the Quality Checks and, when enabled, the kit-file gate and qa; log `Phase 5 APPROVED (lite route, no separate audit)`; then Archive as in Phase 5.
+- Then read `phases:` for Phase 6 and Phase 7 as in `SKILL.md`.
+
+A lite goal that grows past the rubric during work (a fourth file, a shared interface, a new dependency, a destructive, security or infrastructure surface) switches to `full`: set `route: full` in `goal.md`, log the switch with `_kit/log-spawn.sh note`, and continue with the full phases from the current point (Phase 3 evaluation of the goal and tasks, then Phase 5 audit).
